# CODEOWNERS — GitHub requests review from the owners listed here whenever a
# pull request touches a matching path. The last matching rule wins, so the
# default sits first and the per-path rules follow.
#
# This both requests review and requires it. A ruleset on `main` turns on
# `require_code_owner_review`, so a pull request needs an approval from an owner
# of the paths it touches. See docs/branch-protection-settings.md.
#
# Every rule names the same team for now, so any other nke-write member can
# satisfy the requirement. They are kept as the seam for when a
# module gets its own owner, and as a record of the module boundaries. Keep the
# paths honest: the previous `/node-agent/` rule pointed at a directory renamed
# to `agent/` in #36 and matched nothing until this was fixed.

# Default owner for everything not matched below
* @NVIDIA/nke-write

# Cloud Workflow Engine (controller module)
/controller/ @NVIDIA/nke-write

# Agent module — renamed from node-agent in #36
/agent/ @NVIDIA/nke-write

# Build scripts
/build/ @NVIDIA/nke-write

# CI/CD and automation
/.github/ @NVIDIA/nke-write

# Documentation
/docs/ @NVIDIA/nke-write

# Policy files. Same owner as the default today, listed so that routing them
# elsewhere later is a one-line change.
/SECURITY.md @NVIDIA/nke-write
/GOVERNANCE.md @NVIDIA/nke-write
/MAINTAINERS.md @NVIDIA/nke-write
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md @NVIDIA/nke-write
/LICENSE @NVIDIA/nke-write
